Patches applied on top of the pinned upstream RNNoise commit by
scripts/vendor-rnnoise.sh, in filename order.

Local patches:

- `0001-initialize-buffer-model-file.patch` initialises the `file` member in
  `rnnoise_model_from_buffer`. Upstream leaves it as allocator garbage, but
  `rnnoise_model_free` calls `fclose` whenever that member is non-NULL. This
  caused intermittent Linux crashes while closing independently created
  denoisers.
